  "question": {
    "text": "Suppose <math><mi>S</mi></math> and <math><mi>S</mi><mi>′</mi></math> are foci of the ellipse <math><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>25</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math> If <math><mi>P</mi></math> is a variable point on the ellipse and if <math><mo>∆</mo></math> is the area (in sq. units) of the triangle&nbsp;<math><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>′</mi></math>, then the maximum value of&nbsp;<math><mo>∆</mo></math> is double of",
    "image": null
  },
